![Photo by Annie Spratt on Unsplash](cover.jpg)

I find using Artificial Intelligence (Co-Pilot, GPT3 and friends) for
coding, similar to money; a good worker, but a bad boss.

If we rely too much on IA assistance for coding we may loose the
human factor in our projects.

We will become more like a curator, a revisor and corrector of
generated IA code than creators.

Sure, does this means we cannot use libraries or google or
stackoverflow because they can be generated by AI?. It surely we can
not avoid using AI generated code at this point. More and more code
would be influenced by AI in the future.

But you can say that at least the code you are writing is yours.

It's like a Poem.

Maybe human crafted code would be an art in itself. You maybe won't
be able to work properly without AI assistance in the near future,
but at least you can create work of arts 100% human made.

Maybe a Badge like <https://notbyai.fyi/> would help
